{"id":"home-health-state-utilization","title":"Home-health agencies: visits per patient, fast growth and missing State reports","question":"Which San Francisco and Bay Area home-health agencies report far more visits per patient than most, grew fastest, or stopped filing their State utilization report?","finding":"15 San Francisco home-health agencies filed a State utilization report; 1 of them meets a test, and 41 more agencies across the Bay Area do. The middle California agency made 24.4 visits per patient in 2025. Highest in San Francisco: On Lok Senior Health Services (149.8).","how":"From the same State utilization workbooks, report years 2019 to 2025: unduplicated patients and total visits by type of staff; visits per patient only with 20 or more patients. Listed when visits per patient are at least twice the California middle (50 or more patients), visits grew at least ten-fold to 10,000 or more, or the agency is on the non-response list in two of the last three years.","limits":"Agencies that serve people after surgery or with long-term conditions make more visits, and programmes of all-inclusive care for the elderly visit their members often; a new agency grows fast from nothing, and an agency that folds its branches into one licence jumps in a single year; a missing report can mean the agency closed. Medicare pays home health by period of care, so visit counts are a rough guide to cost.","tier":"REDFLAG","columns":[{"k":"agency","t":"Home-health agency","type":"org"},{"k":"city","t":"City","type":"text"},{"k":"county","t":"County","type":"text"},{"k":"year","t":"Latest report year","type":"year"},{"k":"patients","t":"Patients","type":"int"},{"k":"visits","t":"Visits","type":"int"},{"k":"vpp","t":"Visits per patient","type":"times"},{"k":"vppCa","t":"California middle","type":"times"},{"k":"medicareShare","t":"Medicare share of visits","type":"pct"},{"k":"flags","t":"Tests met","type":"text"},{"k":"licensed","t":"Licence effective","type":"date"},{"k":"non